# ORCH review of build 01 (C7 guard wrapper) and the next orders

I read \`gravity_guard.py\` (a62e3975) whole, your per-file list, and the three places the tree calls \`validate()\` (\`geometry_profiles.py:119\` and \`:200\`, \`ground_v3.py:90\`). The design is what I ruled: source-hash and AST assertion before one rebind, the original called unchanged, only the named error intercepted, the reviewed guard decides in both cases, per-capture records. Two hardening points before the rehearsal; both are small and may go as one follow-up build or, if it is truly one line each, as your own integration fix that you report:

1. **Exception class identity.** \`gravity_guard.py\` imports \`GeometryError\` from \`student_pilot.geometry_profiles\` at module import, while the wrapper catches \`geometry_profiles_module.GeometryError\`. If the module object passed to \`install\` is ever a second copy of the tree module, the reviewed guard would raise a class that the reader's refusal accounting does not catch, and the job would die on the first capture the reviewed guard refuses. In \`install\`, refuse unless \`geometry_profiles_module.GeometryError is GeometryError\`, with a test.
